{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I have grown old.</b> Its meaning is after I have grown worn, and the angel spoke truth." "The mem of <b>אמנם</b> is added like the mem of שלשם (Genesis 31:5). And other commentators said that these three men were prophets — and if one should object: was Abraham not a prophet? And how does a prophet come to a prophet, unless he were greater than him in prophecy, like Moses and Aaron? — their answer is that they did not come to Abraham but to Sarah, and so they said, Where is Sarah your wife (Genesis 18:9), and the two went to Sodom. And do not wonder at the phrase for we are destroying (Genesis 19:13), for so it is written, and Moses and Aaron did all the signs (Exodus 11:10) — and HaShem did them and attributed them to them, because they were done through them.\n\nNow, he interpreted and they ate literally. And his interpretation of and he said, Adonai, if now I have found favor (Genesis 18:3) — it is not holy, rather it is like my lords; therefore the nun is open and not kamatz as is its rule. And in the scrolls in which it is kamatz, its meaning would be prophet of HaShem. And the meaning of in your eyes (Genesis 18:3): he spoke first with the greatest of them and afterward with all of them. And we find that the prophet is called angel in Haggai.\n\nAnd some say that Abraham asked permission from the Shekhinah. And some say that it is displaced [muqdam u-me'uḥar], and likewise וישא — now he had already lifted his eyes and done such and such, and afterward HaShem appeared to him and said, Shall I hide from Abraham… also the outcry of Sodom. And these travelers reached Sodom, and Abraham was still standing before HaShem. And in any case, וד׳ אמר (Genesis 18:17) — either He spoke with Abraham or with the angels that they should tell him. But ויאמר ד׳ זעקת סדום (Genesis 18:20) — He spoke with Abraham, and Abraham drew near and said, Will You indeed sweep away (Genesis 18:23).\n\nAnd the verse ויפנו משם האנשים (Genesis 18:22) was inserted to inform that at the time they came to Sodom, then HaShem said to Abraham [about] the outcry of Sodom. Likewise, Say to the young man that he pass on before us… and he passed on, and you stand today (1 Samuel 9:27). And we have no need for scribal emendation [tiqqun soferim]. And the proof is that he said at the end, to the place where he stood there before HaShem (Genesis 19:27). And what is correct in my eyes you will find alluded to in the pericope of ואלה שמות."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The comment is a single continuous block in the source. I have inserted paragraph breaks to reflect the major topical shifts while preserving all content in order."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:05.815533986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}